# K02c negative: the caller's merge result (Bare) has no `value`, which read uses through its hidden input -- the
# source does not carry the field the Consumer reads, so the call is refused (the same admission that admits Other's
# and Wide's results), never read slot 0 of whatever arrived.
Model: (int: value 1)
Bare: (int: other 3)
copy: merge: Model
fn: read () int
return: copy\value
fn: caller () int
    copy: merge: Bare
    return: read()
end: caller
int: result caller()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: result; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
